   "source": [
    "# OpenFOAM Integration with Python\n",
    "\n",
    "## Overview\n",
    "This notebook covers workflows for integrating Python with OpenFOAM. It includes:\n",
    "- Running OpenFOAM solvers from Python\n",
    "- Reading OpenFOAM case data\n",
    "- Post-processing results\n",
    "- Automating CFD workflows\n",
    "\n",
    "## Why OpenFOAM Integration for Engineering?\n",
    "- Automate CFD simulations\n",
    "- Integrate with optimization loops\n",
    "- Process large datasets efficiently\n",
    "- Build digital twins"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setting Up the Environment\n",
    "\n",
    "OpenFOAM requires specific environment variables. This section shows how to set up the environment from Python."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import subprocess\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1.1 Check if OpenFOAM is installed\n",
    "print(\"=== Checking OpenFOAM Installation ===\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Common OpenFOAM installation paths\n",
    "openfoam_paths = [\n",
    "    \"/usr/lib/openfoam\",\n",
    "    \"/opt/openfoam\",\n",
    "    os.path.expanduser(\"~/OpenFOAM\"),\n",
    "    \"/usr/local/lib/openfoam\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "openfoam_found = False\n",
    "for path in openfoam_paths:\n",
    "    if os.path.exists(path):\n",
    "        print(f\"Found OpenFOAM at: {path}\")\n",
    "        openfoam_found = True\n",
    "        break\n",
    "\n",
    "if not openfoam_found:\n",
    "    print(\"OpenFOAM not found in common paths.\")\n",
    "    print(\"Please ensure OpenFOAM is installed and the environment is set up.\")\n",
    "    print(\"\\nTo set up the environment manually:\")\n",
    "    print(\"  source /usr/lib/openfoam/openfoam2406/etc/bashrc  # Adjust path as needed\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"\\nOpenFOAM environment should be available.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 1.2 Source the OpenFOAM environment\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== Sourcing OpenFOAM Environment ===\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Function to source OpenFOAM environment\n",
    "def source_openfoam():\n",
    "    \"\"\"Source the OpenFOAM environment\"\"\"\n",
    "    # Try common OpenFOAM versions\n",
    "    openfoam_versions = [\n",
    "        \"openfoam2406\",\n",
    "        \"openfoam2312\",\n",
    "        \"openfoam2306\",\n",
    "        \"openfoam2302\",\n",
    "        \"openfoam2212\"\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for version in openfoam_versions:\n",
    "        bashrc_path = f\"/usr/lib/openfoam/{version}/etc/bashrc\"\n",
    "        if os.path.exists(bashrc_path):\n",
    "            print(f\"Sourcing: {bashrc_path}\")\n",
    "            # Source the bashrc file\n",
    "            subprocess.run([\"bash\", \"-c\", f\"source {bashrc_path} && env\"], \n",
    "                          capture_output=True, text=True)\n",
    "            return True\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(\"Could not find OpenFOAM bashrc file.\")\n",
    "    return False\n",
    "\n",
    "# Try to source the environment\n",
    "source_openfoam()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
